Programs that nabic links contain the Nabi runtime (lib/libnabir.a) and,
for the targets named below, the C runtime pieces of that target. When you
distribute such a program, the notices of what it contains apply to it:
Rust core and compiler_builtins always; musl for *-linux-musl*; wasi-libc
for wasm32-*; FreeBSD's crt objects for *-freebsd. glibc's crt objects
carry a linking exception and need no notice in a linked program.

